  "response": "### AI Query Simulator Implementation Summary\n\nI have successfully added the **AI Query Simulator** to the Authority Audit page, utilizing the existing Career Graph as the single source of truth.\n\n---\n\n#### 📁 Files Changed / Created\n- **`components/AIQuerySimulator.tsx` (Created)**: Stateful client component that implements the interactive AI Query Simulator.\n- **`app/authority-audit/page.tsx` (Modified)**: Integrated the `<AIQuerySimulator />` island directly between the Live Graph Contract terminal and the Stats Map.\n\n---\n\n#### 🧠 Semantic Graph & Logical Impact\n- **Single Source of Truth**: The component directly queries `lib/career-graph.ts` using established semantic models and helper functions (`evidenceForExpertise`, `decisionsForExpertise`, `citationForExpertise`, `sourceForEvidence`). No mock or external database records are added, ensuring complete data consistency.\n- **Traceable Authority Pathway**: For each of the 6 core expertises, a typical AI query is simulated and mapped step-by-step:\n  1. **AI Input Query & Analytical Intent**: What an LLM/agent seeks.\n  2. **Semantic Alignment (Expertise)**: Matching name, statement, claim, and decision pattern.\n  3. **Conceptual Authority (Citation Surface)**: Core principle, reasoning background (`why`), and explicit boundary constraints (`exception`).\n  4. **Reasoning Nodes (Decisions)**: Concrete real-world decisions made in case studies, linking out to cases.\n  5. **Verifiable Proof (Evidence & Provenance)**: Factual metric logs, their original provenance source link, and verification status.\n  6. **Semantic Knowledge Correlations**: Related blog post links.\n  7. **Resolution/Synthesis**: Final logical compilation verifying why the author has grounded authority on this topic.\n\n---\n\n#### 🧪 Validation Performed\n- Ran `npm run validate` which executes:\n  - **`npm run validate:graph`**: Career Graph Integrity checks passed with `Expertise 6 | Decisions 4 | Evidence 8 | Knowledge 11`.\n  - **`next lint`**: 0 linter errors.\n  - **`npm run lint:blog`** & **`npm run test:frontmatter`**: Frontmatter tests passed.\n  - **`next build`**: Successful Next.js optimized production build with zero static generation or runtime rendering errors.\n- **Mobile responsiveness**: Styled with Tailwind flex-direction, layouts, and font clamps to render beautifully on mobile breakpoints (buttons stack vertically, side-by-side grid shifts to single-column list).\n- **Reduced-motion friendliness**: Interactive paths leverage instant CSS transitions with zero continuous flashing or translational animations, ensuring full compliance with reduced-motion requirements.\n\n---\n\n#### ⚠️ Unresolved Risks\n- **None**: Structural integrity, crawler/discovery routes, and validation scripts remain 100% compliant. No files were bypassed or suppressed.",
